# SPA fallback. The client routes on real paths (/login, /explore,
# /<projectId>), reading window.location.pathname rather than a hash, so a
# static host that looks for a file at that path returns 404 on every direct
# link, refresh, or shared project URL -- only "/" would work.
#
# Lives in public/ so Vite copies it into dist/, which is the directory
# Cloudflare Pages actually publishes. netlify.toml expresses the same rule
# for Netlify; Cloudflare doesn't read that file.
/*    /index.html   200
